      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stroudsburg was founded by Revolutionary War Colonel Jacob Stroud and officially incorporated in 1815.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.poconomountains.com/plan-your-vacation/explore-our-area/stroudsburg/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s location at the confluence of the Pocono, McMichaels, and Brodhead creeks made it a natural spot for early gristmills and sawmills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpa.com/explore/regions/pocono-mountains/stroudsburg/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Downtown Stroudsburg’s streets are lined with slate sidewalks and historic buildings that give the area a charming, walkable feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpa.com/explore/regions/pocono-mountains/stroudsburg/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Stroudsburg serves as the county seat of Monroe County, Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stroudsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Monroe County Historical Association operates out of the Stroud Mansion, once home to Jacob Stroud’s son Daniel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.poconomountains.com/plan-your-vacation/explore-our-area/stroudsburg/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Until the mid‑1960s, the Delaware, Lackawanna and Western Railroad ran trains like the Phoebe Snow through Stroudsburg.",
